ire: </b>MBEDTLS_ECP_INTERNAL_ALT
MBEDTLS_ECP_RANDOMIZE_MXZ_ALT|MBEDTLS_ECP_RANDOMIZE_MXZ_ALT|Functions||||Expose a part of the internal interface of the Elliptic Curve Point module. Support for Weierstrass curves with Jacobi representation MBEDTLS_ECP__FUNCTION_NAME__ALT: Uncomment a macro to let mbed TLS use your * alternative core implementation of elliptic curve arithmetic. Keep in mind that function prototypes should remain the same. This partially replaces one function. The header file from mbed TLS is still used, in contrast to the MBEDTLS_ECP_ALT flag. The original implementation is still present and it is used for group structures not supported by the alternative. Any of these options become available by defining MBEDTLS_ECP_INTERNAL_ALT and implementing the following functions: unsigned char mbedtls_internal_ecp_grp_capable( const mbedtls_ecp_group *grp ) int mbedtls_internal_ecp_init( const mbedtls_ecp_group *grp ) void mbedtls_internal_ecp_deinit( const mbedtls_ecp_group *grp ) The mbedtls_internal_ecp_grp_capable function should return 1 if the replacement functions implement arithmetic for the given group and 0 otherwise. The functions mbedtls_internal_ecp_init and mbedtls_internal_ecp_deinit are called before and after each point operation and provide an opportunity to implement optimized set up and tear down instructions. Example: In case you uncomment MBEDTLS_ECP_INTERNAL_ALT and MBEDTLS_ECP_DOUBLE_JAC_ALT, mbed TLS will still provide the ecp_double_jac function, but will use your mbedtls_internal_ecp_double_jac if the group is supported (your mbedtls_internal_ecp_grp_capable function returns 1 when receives it as an argument). If the group is not supported then the original implementation is used. The other functions and the definition of mbedtls_ecp_group and mbedtls_ecp_point will not change, so your implementation of mbedtls_internal_ecp_double_jac and mbedtls_internal_ecp_grp_capable must be compatible with this definition. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require: </b>MBEDTLS_ECP_INTERNAL_ALT
MBEDTLS_ECP_NORMALIZE_MXZ_ALT|MBEDTLS_ECP_NORMALIZE_MXZ_ALT|Functions||||Expose a part of the internal interface of the Elliptic Curve Point module. Support for Weierstrass curves with Jacobi representation MBEDTLS_ECP__FUNCTION_NAME__ALT: Uncomment a macro to let mbed TLS use your * alternative core implementation of elliptic curve arithmetic. Keep in mind that function prototypes should remain the same. This partially replaces one function. The header file from mbed TLS is still used, in contrast to the MBEDTLS_ECP_ALT flag. The original implementation is still present and it is used for group structures not supported by the alternative. Any of these options become available by defining MBEDTLS_ECP_INTERNAL_ALT and implementing the following functions: unsigned char mbedtls_internal_ecp_grp_capable( const mbedtls_ecp_group *grp ) int mbedtls_internal_ecp_init( const mbedtls_ecp_group *grp ) void mbedtls_internal_ecp_deinit( const mbedtls_ecp_group *grp ) The mbedtls_internal_ecp_grp_capable function should return 1 if the replacement functions implement arithmetic for the given group and 0 otherwise. The functions mbedtls_internal_ecp_init and mbedtls_internal_ecp_deinit are called before and after each point operation and provide an opportunity to implement optimized set up and tear down instructions. Example: In case you uncomment MBEDTLS_ECP_INTERNAL_ALT and MBEDTLS_ECP_DOUBLE_JAC_ALT, mbed TLS will still provide the ecp_double_jac function, but will use your mbedtls_internal_ecp_double_jac if the group is supported (your mbedtls_internal_ecp_grp_capable function returns 1 when receives it as an argument). If the group is not supported then the original implementation is used. The other functions and the definition of mbedtls_ecp_group and mbedtls_ecp_point will not change, so your implementation of mbedtls_internal_ecp_double_jac and mbedtls_internal_ecp_grp_capable must be compatible with this definition. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require: </b>MBEDTLS_ECP_INTERNAL_ALT
MBEDTLS_TEST_NULL_ENTROPY|MBEDTLS_TEST_NULL_ENTROPY|General||||Enables testing and use of mbed TLS without any configured entropy sources. This permits use of the library on platforms before an entropy source has been integrated (see for example the MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_HARDWARE_ALT or the MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_NV_SEED switches). WARNING! This switch MUST be disabled in production builds, and is suitable only for development. Enabling the switch negates any security provided by the library. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_C & MBEDTLS_NO_DEFAULT_ENTROPY_SOURCES
MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_HARDWARE_ALT|MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_HARDWARE_ALT|Platform||||Your own implementation of a hardware entropy collector. Your function must be called \c mbedtls_hardware_poll(), have the same prototype as declared in entropy_poll.h, and accept NULL as first argument. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_AES_FEWER_TABLES|MBEDTLS_AES_FEWER_TABLES|General||||Use less ROM/RAM for AES tables. Uncommenting this macro omits 75% of the AES tables from ROM / RAM (depending on the value of \c MBEDTLS_AES_ROM_TABLES) by computing their values on the fly during operations (the tables are entry-wise rotations of one another). Tradeoff: Uncommenting this reduces the RAM / ROM footprint by ~6kb but at the cost of more arithmetic operations during runtime. Specifically, one has to compare 4 accesses within different tables to 4 accesses with additional arithmetic operations within the same table. The performance gain/loss depends on the system and memory details. This option is independent of \c MBEDTLS_AES_ROM_TABLES. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_AES_ROM_TABLES|MBEDTLS_AES_ROM_TABLES|General||||Store the AES tables in ROM <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_CAMELLIA_SMALL_MEMORY|MBEDTLS_CAMELLIA_SMALL_MEMORY|General||||Use less ROM for the Camellia implementation (saves about 768 bytes). <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_CIPHER_MODE_CBC|MBEDTLS_CIPHER_MODE_CBC|Ciphering||||Enable Cipher Block Chaining mode (CBC) for symmetric ciphers. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CIPHER_MODE_CFB|MBEDTLS_CIPHER_MODE_CFB|Ciphering||||Enable Cipher Feedback mode (CFB) for symmetric ciphers <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CIPHER_MODE_CTR|MBEDTLS_CIPHER_MODE_CTR|Ciphering||||Enable Counter Block Cipher mode (CTR) for symmetric ciphers <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CIPHER_MODE_OFB|MBEDTLS_CIPHER_MODE_OFB|Ciphering||||Enable Output Feedback mode (OFB) for symmetric ciphers. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CIPHER_MODE_XTS|MBEDTLS_CIPHER_MODE_XTS|Ciphering||||Enable Xor-encrypt-xor with ciphertext stealing mode (XTS) for AES. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CIPHER_NULL_CIPHER|MBEDTLS_CIPHER_NULL_CIPHER|Ciphering||||Enable NULL cipher. WARNING!: Only do so when you know what you are doing. This allows for encryption or channels without any security! Requires MBEDTLS_ENABLE_WEAK_CIPHERSUITES as well to enable the following ciphersuites: MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_NULL_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_NULL_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_NULL_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_NULL_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_NULL_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_NULL_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_NULL_MD5 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_NULL_SHA <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_CIPHER_PADDING_PKCS7|MBEDTLS_CIPHER_PADDING_PKCS7|Ciphering||||MBEDTLS_CIPHER_PADDING_XXX: support for specific padding modes in the cipher layer with cipher modes that support padding (e.g. CBC) If you disable all padding modes, only full blocks can be used with CBC. Enable padding modes in the cipher layer. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CIPHER_PADDING_ONE_AND_ZEROS|MBEDTLS_CIPHER_PADDING_ONE_AND_ZEROS|Ciphering||||MBEDTLS_CIPHER_PADDING_XXX: support for specific padding modes in the cipher layer with cipher modes that support padding (e.g. CBC) If you disable all padding modes, only full blocks can be used with CBC. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CIPHER_PADDING_ZEROS_AND_LEN|MBEDTLS_CIPHER_PADDING_ZEROS_AND_LEN|Ciphering||||Uncomment or comment macros to add support for specific padding modes in the cipher layer with cipher modes that support padding (e.g. CBC) If you disable all padding modes, only full blocks can be used with CBC. Enable padding modes in the cipher layer. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CIPHER_PADDING_ZEROS|MBEDTLS_CIPHER_PADDING_ZEROS|Ciphering||||MBEDTLS_CIPHER_PADDING_XXX: support for specific padding modes in the cipher layer with cipher modes that support padding (e.g. CBC) If you disable all padding modes, only full blocks can be used with CBC. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ENABLE_WEAK_CIPHERSUITES|MBEDTLS_ENABLE_WEAK_CIPHERSUITES|Ciphering||||Enable weak ciphersuites in SSL / TLS WARNING!: Only do so when you know what you are doing. This allows for channels with virtually no security at all! This enables the following ciphersuites: MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_DES_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_DES_CBC_SHA \warning DES is considered a weak cipher and its use constitutes a security risk. We recommend considering stronger ciphers instead. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_REMOVE_ARC4_CIPHERSUITES|MBEDTLS_REMOVE_ARC4_CIPHERSUITES|Ciphering||||Remove RC4 ciphersuites by default in SSL / TLS. This flag removes the ciphersuites based on RC4 from the default list as returned by mbedtls_ssl_list_ciphersuites(). However, it is still possible to enable (some of) them with mbedtls_ssl_conf_ciphersuites() by including them explicitly. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_REMOVE_3DES_CIPHERSUITES|MBEDTLS_REMOVE_3DES_CIPHERSUITES|Ciphering||||Remove 3DES ciphersuites by default in SSL / TLS. This flag removes the ciphersuites based on 3DES from the default list as returned by mbedtls_ssl_list_ciphersuites(). However, it is still possible to enable (some of) them with mbedtls_ssl_conf_ciphersuites() by including them explicitly. A man-in-the-browser attacker can recover authentication tokens sent through a TLS connection using a 3DES based cipher suite (see "On the Practical(In-)Security of 64-bit Block Ciphers" by Karthikeyan Bhargavan and Gaëtan Leurent, see https://sweet32.info/SWEET32_CCS16.pdf). If this attack falls in your threat model or you are unsure, then you should keep this option enabled to remove 3DES based cipher suites. Comment this macro to keep 3DES in the default ciphersuite list. <b>Default value: </b>Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP192R1_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP192R1_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP224R1_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP224R1_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP256R1_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP256R1_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP384R1_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP384R1_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP521R1_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP521R1_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP192K1_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP192K1_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP224K1_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP224K1_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP256K1_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP256K1_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP256R1_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP256R1_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP384R1_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP384R1_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP512R1_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP512R1_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_CURVE25519_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_CURVE25519_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_CURVE448_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_CURVE448_ENABLED|Elliptic curves||||Enables this specific curve within the Elliptic Curve module. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_NIST_OPTIM|MBEDTLS_ECP_NIST_OPTIM|General||||Enable specific 'modulo p' routines for each NIST prime. Depending on the prime and architecture, makes operations 4 to 8 times faster on the corresponding curve. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECP_RESTARTABLE|MBEDTLS_ECP_RESTARTABLE|General||||Enable "non-blocking" ECC operations that can return early and be resumed. This allows various functions to pause by returning #MBEDTLS_ERR_ECP_IN_PROGRESS (or, for functions in the SSL module, #MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_CRYPTO_IN_PROGRESS) and then be called later again in order to further progress and eventually complete their operation. This is controlled through mbedtls_ecp_set_max_ops() which limits the maximum number of ECC operations a function may perform before pausing; see mbedtls_ecp_set_max_ops() for more information. This is useful in non-threaded environments if you want to avoid blocking for too long on ECC (and, hence, X.509 or SSL/TLS) operations. Uncomment this macro to enable restartable ECC computations. note: This option only works with the default software implementation of elliptic curve functionality. It is incompatible with MBEDTLS_ECP_ALT, MBEDTLS_ECDH_XXX_ALT and MBEDTLS_ECDSA_XXX_ALT. <b>Default value:</b> Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_ECDSA_DETERMINISTIC|MBEDTLS_ECDSA_DETERMINISTIC|General||||Enable deterministic ECDSA (RFC 6979). Standard ECDSA is ""fragile"" in the sense that lack of entropy when signing may result in a compromise of the long-term signing key. This is avoided by the deterministic variant. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_HMAC_DRBG_C
MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_PSK_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_PSK_ENABLED|Key exchange||||Enable the PSK based ciphersuite modes in SSL / TLS. This enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_RC4_128_SHA <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_DHE_PSK_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_DHE_PSK_ENABLED|Key exchange||||Enable the DHE-PSK based ciphersuite modes in SSL / TLS. This enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_RC4_128_SHA \warning Using DHE constitutes a security risk as it is not possible to validate custom DH parameters. If possible, it is recommended users should consider preferring other methods of key exchange. See dhm.h for more details. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_DHM_C
MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDHE_PSK_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDHE_PSK_ENABLED|Key exchange||||Enable the ECDHE-PSK based ciphersuite modes in SSL / TLS. This enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256vMBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_RC4_128_SHA <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ECDH_C
MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_RSA_PSK_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_RSA_PSK_ENABLED|Key exchange||||Enable the RSA-PSK based ciphersuite modes in SSL / TLS. This enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_RC4_128_SHA <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_RSA_C & MBEDTLS_PKCS1_V15 & MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_PARSE_C
MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_RSA_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_RSA_ENABLED|Key exchange||||Enable the RSA-only based ciphersuite modes in SSL / TLS. This enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_RC4_128_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_RC4_128_MD5 <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_RSA_C & MBEDTLS_PKCS1_V15 & MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_PARSE_C
MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_DHE_RSA_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_DHE_RSA_ENABLED|Key exchange||||Enable the DHE-RSA based ciphersuite modes in SSL / TLS. This enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA \warning Using DHE constitutes a security risk as it is not possible to validate custom DH parameters. If possible, it is recommended users should consider preferring other methods of key exchange. See dhm.h for more details.<b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_DHM_C & MBEDTLS_RSA_C & MBEDTLS_PKCS1_V15 & MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_PARSE_C
MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDHE_RSA_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDHE_RSA_ENABLED|Key exchange||||Enable the ECDHE-RSA based ciphersuite modes in SSL / TLS. This enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_RC4_128_SHA <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ECDH_C & MBEDTLS_RSA_C & MBEDTLS_PKCS1_V15 & MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_PARSE_C
MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDHE_ECDSA_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDHE_ECDSA_ENABLED|Key exchange||||Enable the ECDHE-ECDSA based ciphersuite modes in SSL / TLS. This enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_RC4_128_SHA <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ECDH_C & MBEDTLS_ECDSA_C & MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_PARSE_C
MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDH_ECDSA_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDH_ECDSA_ENABLED|Key exchange||||Enable the ECDH-ECDSA based ciphersuite modes in SSL / TLS. This enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_RC4_128_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ECDH_C & MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_PARSE_C
MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDH_RSA_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDH_RSA_ENABLED|Key exchange||||Enable the ECDH-RSA based ciphersuite modes in SSL / TLS. This enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_RC4_128_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ECDH_C & MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_PARSE_C
MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECJPAKE_ENABLED|MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECJPAKE_ENABLED|Key exchange||||Enable the ECJPAKE based ciphersuite modes in SSL / TLS. WARNING! This is currently experimental. EC J-PAKE support is based on the Thread v1.0.0 specification; incompatible changes to the specification might still happen. For this reason, this is disabled by default. This enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_ECJPAKE_WITH_AES_128_CCM_8 <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ECJPAKE_C & MBEDTLS_SHA256_C & MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP256R1_ENABLED
MBEDTLS_PK_PARSE_EC_EXTENDED|MBEDTLS_PK_PARSE_EC_EXTENDED|General||||Enhance support for reading EC keys using variants of SEC1 not allowed by RFC 5915 and RFC 5480. Currently this means parsing the SpecifiedECDomain choice of EC parameters (only known groups are supported, not arbitrary domains, to avoid validation issues). Disable if you only need to support RFC 5915 + 5480 key formats. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ERROR_STRERROR_DUMMY|MBEDTLS_ERROR_STRERROR_DUMMY|General||||Enable a dummy error function to make use of mbedtls_strerror() in third party libraries easier when MBEDTLS_ERROR_C is disabled (no effect when MBEDTLS_ERROR_C is enabled). You can safely disable this if MBEDTLS_ERROR_C is enabled, or if you're not using mbedtls_strerror() or error_strerror() in your application. Disable if you run into name conflicts and want to really remove the mbedtls_strerror() <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_GENPRIME|MBEDTLS_GENPRIME|General||||Enable the prime-number generation code. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_BIGNUM_C
MBEDTLS_FS_IO|MBEDTLS_FS_IO|General||||Enable functions that use the filesystem. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_NO_DEFAULT_ENTROPY_SOURCES|MBEDTLS_NO_DEFAULT_ENTROPY_SOURCES|General||||Do not add default entropy sources. These are the platform specific, mbedtls_timing_hardclock and HAVEGE based poll functions. This is useful to have more control over the added entropy sources in an application. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) when RNG is not activated It can be set to disabled, but this means that the mbedtls library will be built either: - without any random number generator, which will make the application vulnerable - with a pure SW random number generator, if the flag “MBEDTLS_HAVEGE_C” is set, but this will be costly in term of CPU and SIZE.
MBEDTLS_NO_PLATFORM_ENTROPY|MBEDTLS_NO_PLATFORM_ENTROPY|General||||Do not use built-in platform entropy functions. This is useful if your platform does not support standards like the /dev/urandom or Windows CryptoAPI. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_FORCE_SHA256|MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_FORCE_SHA256|General||||Force the entropy accumulator to use a SHA-256 accumulator instead of the default SHA-512 based one (if both are available). On 32-bit systems SHA-256 can be much faster than SHA-512. Use this option if you have performance concerns. This option is only useful if both MBEDTLS_SHA256_C and MBEDTLS_SHA512_C are defined. Otherwise the available hash module is used. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SHA256_C
MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_NV_SEED|MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_NV_SEED|General||||Enable the non-volatile (NV) seed file-based entropy source. (Also enables the NV seed read/write functions in the platform layer). This is crucial (if not required) on systems that do not have a cryptographic entropy source (in hardware or kernel) available. <b>Note:</b> The read/write functions that are used by the entropy source are determined in the platform layer, and can be modified at runtime and/or compile-time depending on the flags (MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_NV_SEED_*) used. <b>Note:</b> If you use the default implementation functions that read a seedfile with regular fopen(), please make sure you make a seedfile with the proper name (defined in MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_STD_NV_SEED_FILE) and at least MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_BLOCK_SIZE bytes in size that can be read from and written to or you will get an entropy source error! The default implementation will only use the first MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_BLOCK_SIZE bytes from the file. <b>Note:</b> The entropy collector will write to the seed file before entropy is given to an external source, to update it. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_C & MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_C
MBEDTLS_MEMORY_DEBUG|MBEDTLS_MEMORY_DEBUG|General||||Enable debugging of buffer allocator memory issues. Automatically prints (to stderr) all (fatal) messages on memory allocation issues. Enables function for 'debug output' of allocated memory. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_MEMORY_BUFFER_ALLOC_C
MBEDTLS_MEMORY_BACKTRACE|MBEDTLS_MEMORY_BACKTRACE|General||||Include backtrace information with each allocated block. Require GLIBC-compatible backtrace and backtrace_symbols() support <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_MEMORY_BUFFER_ALLOC_C
MBEDTLS_PK_RSA_ALT_SUPPORT|MBEDTLS_PK_RSA_ALT_SUPPORT|General||||Support external private RSA keys (eg from a HSM) in the PK layer. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_PKCS1_V15|MBEDTLS_PKCS1_V15|General||||Enable support for PKCS#1 v1.5 encoding. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_RSA_C (This enables support for PKCS#1 v1.5 operations.)
MBEDTLS_PKCS1_V21|MBEDTLS_PKCS1_V21|General||||Enable support for PKCS#1 v2.1 encoding. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_MD_C & MBEDTLS_RSA_C (This enables support for RSAES-OAEP and RSASSA-PSS operations.)
MBEDTLS_RSA_NO_CRT|MBEDTLS_RSA_NO_CRT|General||||Do not use the Chinese Remainder Theorem for the RSA private operation. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_SELF_TEST|MBEDTLS_SELF_TEST|General||||Enable the checkup functions (*_self_test). <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SHA256_SMALLER|MBEDTLS_SHA256_SMALLER|General||||Enable an implementation of SHA-256 that has lower ROM footprint but also lower performance. The default implementation is meant to be a reasonnable compromise between performance and size. This version optimizes more aggressively for size at the expense of performance. Eg on Cortex-M4 it reduces the size of mbedtls_sha256_process() from ~2KB to ~0.5KB for a performance hit of about 30%. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_ALL_ALERT_MESSAGES|MBEDTLS_SSL_ALL_ALERT_MESSAGES|SSL||||Enable sending of alert messages in case of encountered errors as per RFC. If you choose not to send the alert messages, mbed TLS can still communicate with other servers, only debugging of failures is harder. The advantage of not sending alert messages, is that no information is given about reasons for failures thus preventing adversaries of gaining intel. Enable sending of all alert messages <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_ASYNC_PRIVATE|MBEDTLS_SSL_ASYNC_PRIVATE|SSL||||Enable asynchronous external private key operations in SSL. This allows you to configure an SSL connection to call an external cryptographic module to perform private key operations instead of performing the operation inside the library. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_DEBUG_ALL|MBEDTLS_SSL_DEBUG_ALL|SSL||||Enable the debug messages in SSL module for all issues. Debug messages have been disabled in some places to prevent timing attacks due to (unbalanced) debugging function calls. If you need all error reporting(debug messages on errors introducing a timing side-channel) you should enable this during debugging, but remove this for production servers that should log as well. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_ENCRYPT_THEN_MAC|MBEDTLS_SSL_ENCRYPT_THEN_MAC|SSL||||Enable support for Encrypt-then-MAC, RFC 7366. This allows peers that both support it to use a more robust protection for ciphersuites using CBC, providing deep resistance against timing attacks on the padding or underlying cipher. This only affects CBC ciphersuites, and is useless if none is defined. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1 / MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_1 / MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_2
MBEDTLS_SSL_EXTENDED_MASTER_SECRET|MBEDTLS_SSL_EXTENDED_MASTER_SECRET|SSL||||Enable support for Extended Master Secret, aka Session Hash (draft-ietf-tls-session-hash-02). This was introduced as ""the proper fix"" to the Triple Handshake familiy of attacks, but it is recommended to always use it (even if you disable renegotiation), since it actually fixes a more fundamental issue in the original SSL/TLS design, and has implications beyond Triple Handshake. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1 / MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_1 / MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_2
MBEDTLS_SSL_FALLBACK_SCSV|MBEDTLS_SSL_FALLBACK_SCSV|SSL||||Enable support for FALLBACK_SCSV (draft-ietf-tls-downgrade-scsv-00). For servers, it is recommended to always enable this, unless you support only one version of TLS, or know for sure that none of your clients implements a fallback strategy. For clients, you only need this if you're using a fallback strategy, which is not recommended in the first place, unless you absolutely need it to interoperate with buggy (version-intolerant) servers. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_HW_RECORD_ACCEL|MBEDTLS_SSL_HW_RECORD_ACCEL|SSL||||Enable hooking functions in SSL module for hardware acceleration of individual records. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_CBC_RECORD_SPLITTING|MBEDTLS_SSL_CBC_RECORD_SPLITTING|SSL||||Enable 1/n-1 record splitting for CBC mode in SSLv3 and TLS 1.0. This is a countermeasure to the BEAST attack, which also minimizes the risk of interoperability issues compared to sending 0-length records. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_RENEGOTIATION|MBEDTLS_SSL_RENEGOTIATION|SSL||||Disable support for TLS renegotiation. The two main uses of renegotiation are (1) refresh keys on long-lived connections and (2) client authentication after the initial handshake. If you don't need renegotiation, it's probably better to disable it, since it has been associated with security issues in the past and is easy to misuse/misunderstand. \note Even if this option is disabled, both client and server are aware of the Renegotiation Indication Extension (RFC 5746) used to prevent the SSL renegotiation attack (see RFC 5746 Sect. 1). (See \c mbedtls_ssl_conf_legacy_renegotiation for the configuration of this extension). <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_SRV_SUPPORT_SSLV2_CLIENT_HELLO|MBEDTLS_SSL_SRV_SUPPORT_SSLV2_CLIENT_HELLO|SSL||||Enable support for receiving and parsing SSLv2 Client Hello messages for the SSL Server module (MBEDTLS_SSL_SRV_C). <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_SRV_RESPECT_CLIENT_PREFERENCE|MBEDTLS_SSL_SRV_RESPECT_CLIENT_PREFERENCE|SSL||||Pick the ciphersuite according to the client's preferences rather than ours in the SSL Server module (MBEDTLS_SSL_SRV_C). <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_MAX_FRAGMENT_LENGTH|MBEDTLS_SSL_MAX_FRAGMENT_LENGTH|SSL||||Enable support for RFC 6066 max_fragment_length extension in SSL. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_SSL3|MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_SSL3|SSL||||Enable support for SSL 3.0. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_MD5_C & MBEDTLS_SHA1_C
MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1|MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1|SSL||||Enable support for TLS 1.0. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_MD5_C & MBEDTLS_SHA1_C
MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_1|MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_1|SSL||||Enable support for TLS 1.1 (and DTLS 1.0 if DTLS is enabled). <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_MD5_C & MBEDTLS_SHA1_C
MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_2|MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_2|SSL||||<b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SHA1_C or MBEDTLS_SHA256_C or MBEDTLS_SHA512_C
MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_DTLS|MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_DTLS|SSL||||Enable support for DTLS (all available versions). Enable this and MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_1 to enable DTLS 1.0, and/or this and MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_2 to enable DTLS 1.2. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_1 / MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_2
MBEDTLS_SSL_ALPN|MBEDTLS_SSL_ALPN|SSL||||Enable support for RFC 7301 Application Layer Protocol Negotiation. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_DTLS_ANTI_REPLAY|MBEDTLS_SSL_DTLS_ANTI_REPLAY|SSL||||Enable support for the anti-replay mechanism in DTLS. Warning! Disabling this is often a security risk! See mbedtls_ssl_conf_dtls_anti_replay() for details. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS_C & MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_DTLS
MBEDTLS_SSL_DTLS_HELLO_VERIFY|MBEDTLS_SSL_DTLS_HELLO_VERIFY|SSL||||Enable support for HelloVerifyRequest on DTLS servers. This feature is highly recommended to prevent DTLS servers being used as amplifiers in DoS attacks against other hosts. It should always be enabled unless you know for sure amplification cannot be a problem in the environment in which your server operates. WARNING! Disabling this is often a security risk! <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_DTLS
MBEDTLS_SSL_DTLS_CLIENT_PORT_REUSE|MBEDTLS_SSL_DTLS_CLIENT_PORT_REUSE|SSL||||Enable server-side support for clients that reconnect from the same port. Some clients unexpectedly close the connection and try to reconnect using the same source port. This needs special support from the server to handle the new connection securely, as described in section 4.2.8 of RFC 6347. This flag enables that support. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SSL_DTLS_HELLO_VERIFY
MBEDTLS_SSL_DTLS_BADMAC_LIMIT|MBEDTLS_SSL_DTLS_BADMAC_LIMIT|SSL||||Enable support for a limit of records with bad MAC. See mbedtls_ssl_conf_dtls_badmac_limit(). <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_DTLS
MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS|MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS|SSL||||Enable support for RFC 5077 session tickets in SSL. Client-side, provides full support for session tickets (maintainance of a session store remains the responsibility of the application, though). Server-side, you also need to provide callbacks for writing and parsing tickets, including authenticated encryption and key management. Example callbacks are provided by MBEDTLS_SSL_TICKET_C. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_EXPORT_KEYS|MBEDTLS_SSL_EXPORT_KEYS|SSL||||Enable support for exporting key block and master secret. This is required for certain users of TLS, e.g. EAP-TLS. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_SERVER_NAME_INDICATION|MBEDTLS_SSL_SERVER_NAME_INDICATION|SSL||||Enable support for RFC 6066 server name indication (SNI) in SSL. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_PARSE_C
MBEDTLS_SSL_TRUNCATED_HMAC|MBEDTLS_SSL_TRUNCATED_HMAC|SSL||||Enable support for RFC 6066 truncated HMAC in SSL. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_TRUNCATED_HMAC_COMPAT|MBEDTLS_SSL_TRUNCATED_HMAC_COMPAT|SSL||||Fallback to old (pre-2.7), non-conforming implementation of the truncated HMAC extension which also truncates the HMAC key. Note that this option is only meant for a transitory upgrade period and is likely to be removed in a future version of the library. \WARNING!: The old implementation is non-compliant and has a security weakness (2^80 brute force attack on the HMAC key used for a single, uninterrupted connection). This should only be enabled temporarily when (1) the use of truncated HMAC is essential in order to save bandwidth, and (2) the peer is an Mbed TLS stack that doesn't use the fixed implementation yet (pre-2.7). \DEPRECATED This option is deprecated and will likely be removed in a future version of Mbed TLS. Uncomment to fallback to old, non-compliant truncated HMAC implementation. <b>Requires:</b> MBEDTLS_SSL_TRUNCATED_HMAC <b>Default value:</b> Not defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_THREADING_ALT|MBEDTLS_THREADING_ALT|General||||Provide your own alternate threading implementation. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_THREADING_C
MBEDTLS_THREADING_PTHREAD|MBEDTLS_THREADING_PTHREAD|General||||Enable the pthread wrapper layer for the threading layer. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_THREADING_C
MBEDTLS_VERSION_FEATURES|MBEDTLS_VERSION_FEATURES|General||||Allow run-time checking of compile-time enabled features. Thus allowing users to check at run-time if the library is for instance compiled with threading support via mbedtls_version_check_feature(). <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_VERSION_C (Disabling it will disable run-time checking and save ROM space)
MBEDTLS_X509_ALLOW_EXTENSIONS_NON_V3|MBEDTLS_X509_ALLOW_EXTENSIONS_NON_V3|X509||||If set, the X509 parser will not break-off when parsing an X509 certificate and encountering an extension in a v1 or v2 certificate. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_X509_ALLOW_UNSUPPORTED_CRITICAL_EXTENSION|MBEDTLS_X509_ALLOW_UNSUPPORTED_CRITICAL_EXTENSION|X509||||If set, the X509 parser will not break-off when parsing an X509 certificate and encountering an unknown critical extension. WARNING! Depending on your PKI use, enabling this can be a security risk! <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_X509_CHECK_KEY_USAGE|MBEDTLS_X509_CHECK_KEY_USAGE|X509||||Enable verification of the keyUsage extension (CA and leaf certificates). Disabling this avoids problems with mis-issued and/or misused (intermediate) CA and leaf certificates. WARNING! Depending on your PKI use, disabling this can be a security risk! <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_X509_CHECK_EXTENDED_KEY_USAGE|MBEDTLS_X509_CHECK_EXTENDED_KEY_USAGE|X509||||Enable verification of the extendedKeyUsage extension (leaf certificates). Disabling this avoids problems with mis-issued and/or isused certificates. WARNING! Depending on your PKI use, disabling this can be a security risk! <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_X509_RSASSA_PSS_SUPPORT|MBEDTLS_X509_RSASSA_PSS_SUPPORT|X509||||Enable parsing and verification of X.509 certificates, CRLs and CSRS signed with RSASSA-PSS (aka PKCS#1 v2.1). <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ZLIB_SUPPORT|MBEDTLS_ZLIB_SUPPORT|General||||If set, the SSL/TLS module uses ZLIB to support compression and decompression of packet data. WARNING! TLS-level compression MAY REDUCE SECURITY! See for example the CRIME attack. Before enabling this option, you should examine with care if CRIME or similar exploits may be a applicable to your use case. <b>Note:</b> Currently compression can't be used with DTLS. \deprecated This feature is deprecated and will be removed in the next major revision of the library. <b>Used in:</b> library/ssl_tls.c library/ssl_cli.c library/ssl_srv.c This feature requires zlib library and headers to be present. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_AESNI_C|MBEDTLS_AESNI_C|General||||Enable AES-NI support on x86-64. Module: library/aesni.c Caller: library/aes.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_HAVE_ASM
MBEDTLS_AES_C|MBEDTLS_AES_C|General||||Enable the AES block cipher. Module: library/aes.c Caller: library/ssl_tls.c library/pem.c library/ctr_drbg.c This module enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA PEM_PARSE uses AES for decrypting encrypted keys. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_HAVE_ASM
MBEDTLS_ARC4_C|MBEDTLS_ARC4_C|General||||Enable the ARCFOUR stream cipher Module: library/arc4.c Caller: library/ssl_tls.c This module enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_RC4_128_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_RC4_128_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_RC4_128_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_RC4_128_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_RC4_128_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_RC4_128_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_RC4_128_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_RC4_128_MD5 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_RC4_128_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_RC4_128_SHA \warning ARC4 is considered a weak cipher and its use constitutes a security risk. If possible, we recommend avoidng dependencies on it, and considering stronger ciphers instead. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ASN1_PARSE_C|MBEDTLS_ASN1_PARSE_C|General||||Enable the generic ASN1 parser Module: library/asn1.c Caller: library/x509.c library/dhm.c library/pkcs12.c library/pkcs5.c library/pkparse.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ASN1_WRITE_C|MBEDTLS_ASN1_WRITE_C|General||||Enable the generic ASN1 writer Module: library/asn1write.c Caller: library/ecdsa.c library/pkwrite.c library/x509_create.c library/x509write_crt.c library/x509write_csr.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_BASE64_C|MBEDTLS_BASE64_C|General||||Enable the Base64 module Module: library/base64.c Caller: library/pem.c This module is required for PEM support (required by X.509). <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_BIGNUM_C|MBEDTLS_BIGNUM_C|General||||Enable the multi-precision integer library Module: library/bignum.c Caller: library/dhm.c library/ecp.c library/ecdsa.c library/rsa.c library/ssl_tls.c This module is required for RSA, DHM and ECC (ECDH, ECDSA) support. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_BLOWFISH_C|MBEDTLS_BLOWFISH_C|General||||Enable the Blowfish block cipher Module: library/blowfish.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CAMELLIA_C|MBEDTLS_CAMELLIA_C|General||||Enable the Camellia block cipher Module: library/camellia.c Caller: library/ssl_tls.c This module enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_CAMELLIA_128_CBC_SHA256 <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ARIA_C|MBEDTLS_ARIA_C|General||||Enable the ARIA block cipher. Module: library/aria.c Caller: library/cipher.c This module enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_ARIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_ARIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_ARIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_ARIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_ARIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_ARIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_ARIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_ARIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_ARIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_ARIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_ARIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_ARIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_ARIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_ARIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_ARIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_ARIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_ARIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_ARIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_ARIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_ARIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_ARIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_ARIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_ARIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_ARIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_ARIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_ARIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_ARIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_ARIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_ARIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_ARIA_256_CBC_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_ARIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_ARIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_ARIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_ARIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_ARIA_128_GCM_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_ARIA_256_GCM_SHA384 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_ARIA_128_CBC_SHA256 MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_ARIA_256_CBC_SHA384 <b>Default value:</b> Not defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_CCM_C|MBEDTLS_CCM_C|General||||Enable the Counter with CBC-MAC (CCM) mode for 128-bit block cipher. Module: library/ccm.c This module enables the AES-CCM ciphersuites, if other requisites areenabled as well. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_AES_C / MBEDTLS_CAMELLIA_C
MBEDTLS_CERTS_C|MBEDTLS_CERTS_C|General||||Enable the test certificates. Used for testing (ssl_client/server) Module: library/certs.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CHACHA20_C|MBEDTLS_CHACHA20_C|General||||Enable the ChaCha20 stream cipher. Module: library/chacha20.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CHACHAPOLY_C|MBEDTLS_CHACHAPOLY_C|General||||Enable the ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD algorithm.. Module: library/chachapoly.c This module requires: MBEDTLS_CHACHA20_C, MBEDTLS_POLY1305_C<b> Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CIPHER_C|MBEDTLS_CIPHER_C|General||||Enable the generic cipher layer Module: library/cipher.c Caller: library/ssl_tls.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_CMAC_C|MBEDTLS_CMAC_C|General||||Enable the CMAC (Cipher-based Message Authentication Code) mode for block ciphers. Module: library/cmac.c <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_AES_C / MBEDTLS_DES_C
MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_C|MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_C|General||||Enable the CTR_DRBG AES-256-based random generator Module: library/ctr_drbg.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_AES_C
MBEDTLS_DEBUG_C|MBEDTLS_DEBUG_C|General||||Enable the debug functions Module: library/debug.c Caller: library/ssl_cli.c library/ssl_srv.c library/ssl_tls.c <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_DES_C|MBEDTLS_DES_C|General||||Enable the DES block cipher Module: library/des.c Caller: library/pem.c library/ssl_tls.c This module enables the following ciphersuites (if other requisites are enabled as well): MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_ECDSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDH_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_DHE_PSK_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_RSA_PSK_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA MBEDTLS_TLS_PSK_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA PEM_PARSE uses DES/3DES for decrypting encrypted keys. \warning DES is considered a weak cipher and its use constitutes a security risk. We recommend considering stronger ciphers instead. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_DHM_C|MBEDTLS_DHM_C|General||||Enable the Diffie-Hellman-Merkle key exchange Module: library/dhm.c Caller: library/ssl_cli.c library/ssl_srv.c This module is used by the following key exchanges: DHE-RSA, DHE-PSK \warning Using DHE constitutes a security risk as it is not possible to validate custom DH parameters. If possible, it is recommended users should consider preferring other methods of key exchange. See dhm.h for more details.<b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_ECDH_C|MBEDTLS_ECDH_C|General||||Enable the elliptic curve Diffie-Hellman library. Module: library/ecdh.c Caller: library/ssl_cli.c library/ssl_srv.c This module is used by the following key exchanges: ECDHE-ECDSA, ECDHE-RSA, DHE-PSK <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ECP_C
MBEDTLS_ECDSA_C|MBEDTLS_ECDSA_C|General||||Enable the elliptic curve DSA library. Module: library/ecdsa.c This module is used by the following key exchanges: ECDHE-ECDSA <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ECP_C & MBEDTLS_ASN1_WRITE_C & MBEDTLS_ASN1_PARSE_C
MBEDTLS_ECJPAKE_C|MBEDTLS_ECJPAKE_C|General||||Enable the elliptic curve J-PAKE library. WARNING! This is currently experimental. EC J-PAKE support is based on the Thread v1.0.0 specification; incompatible changes to the specification might still happen. For this reason, this is disabled by default. Module: library/ecjpake.c This module is used by the following key exchanges: ECJPAKE <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ECP_C & MBEDTLS_MD_C
MBEDTLS_ECP_C|MBEDTLS_ECP_C|General||||Enable the elliptic curve over GF(p) library. Module: library/ecp.c Caller: library/ecdh.c library/ecdsa.c library/ecjpake.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_BIGNUM_C & (MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP192R1_ENABLED / MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP224R1_ENABLED / MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP256R1_ENABLED / MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP384R1_ENABLED / MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP521R1_ENABLED / MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP192K1_ENABLED / MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP224K1_ENABLED / MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_SECP256K1_ENABLED / MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP256R1_ENABLED / MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP384R1_ENABLED / MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_BP512R1_ENABLED / MBEDTLS_ECP_DP_CURVE25519_ENABLED )
MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_C|MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_C|General||||Enable the platform-specific entropy code Module: library/entropy.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SHA512_C / MBEDTLS_SHA256_C
MBEDTLS_ERROR_C|MBEDTLS_ERROR_C|General||||Enable error code to error string conversion Module: library/error.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_GCM_C|MBEDTLS_GCM_C|General||||Enable the Galois/Counter Mode (GCM) for AES Module: library/gcm.c This module enables the AES-GCM and CAMELLIA-GCM ciphersuites, if other requisites are enabled as well. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_AES_C / MBEDTLS_CAMELLIA_C
MBEDTLS_HAVEGE_C|MBEDTLS_HAVEGE_C|General||||Enable the HAVEGE random generator WARNING!: the HAVEGE random generator is not suitable for virtualized environments WARNING!: the HAVEGE random generator is dependent on timing and specific processor traits. It is therefore not advised to use HAVEGE as your applications primary random generator or primary entropy pool input. As a secondary input to your entropy pool, it IS able add the (limited) extra entropy it provides. Module: library/havege.c <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_TIMING_C
MBEDTLS_HKDF_C|MBEDTLS_HKDF_C|General||||Enable the HKDF algorithm (RFC 5869). Module: library/hkdf.c * This module adds support for the Hashed Message Authentication Code(HMAC)-based key derivation function (HKDF). <b>Default value: </b>Defined(define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_MD_C
MBEDTLS_HMAC_DRBG_C|MBEDTLS_HMAC_DRBG_C|General||||Enable the HMAC_DRBG random generator. Module: library/hmac_drbg.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_MD_C
MBEDTLS_NIST_KW_C|MBEDTLS_NIST_KW_C|General||||Enable the Key Wrapping mode for 128-bit block ciphers, as defined in NIST SP 800-38F. Only KW and KWP modes are supported. At the moment, only AES is approved by NIST. Module: library/nist_kw.c <b>Default value:</b> Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_MD_C|MBEDTLS_MD_C|General||||Enable the generic message digest layer Module: library/md.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_MD2_C|MBEDTLS_MD2_C|General||||Enable the MD2 hash algorithm Module: library/md2.c \warning MD2 is considered a weak message digest and its use constitutes a security risk. If possible, we recommend avoiding dependencies on it, and considering stronger message digests instead. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_MD4_C|MBEDTLS_MD4_C|General||||Enable the MD4 hash algorithm Module: library/md4.c \warning MD4 is considered a weak message digest and its use constitutes a security risk. If possible, we recommend avoiding dependencies on it, and considering stronger message digests instead. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_MD5_C|MBEDTLS_MD5_C|General||||Enable the MD5 hash algorithm Module: library/md5.c Caller: library/md.c library/pem.c library/ssl_tls.c This module is required for SSL/TLS up to version 1.1, and for TLS 1.2 depending on the handshake parameters. Further, it is used for checking MD5-signed certificates, and for PBKDF1 when decrypting PEM-encoded encrypted keys. \warning MD5 is considered a weak message digest and its use constitutes a security risk. If possible, we recommend avoiding dependencies on it, and considering stronger message digests instead. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_MEMORY_BUFFER_ALLOC_C|MBEDTLS_MEMORY_BUFFER_ALLOC_C|General||||Enable the buffer allocator implementation that makes use of a (stack) based buffer to 'allocate' dynamic memory. (replaces calloc() and free() calls) Module: library/memory_buffer_alloc.c <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_C & MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_MEMORY
MBEDTLS_NET_C|MBEDTLS_NET_C|General||||Enable the TCP and UDP over IPv6/IPv4 networking routines. Note: This module only works on POSIX/Unix (including Linux, BSD and OS X) and Windows. For other platforms, you'll want to disable it, and write your own networking callbacks to be passed to \c mbedtls_ssl_set_bio().</b><b>Note:</b> See also our Knowledge Base article about porting to a new environment: https://tls.mbed.org/kb/how-to/how-do-i-port-mbed-tls-to-a-new-environment-OS <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_OID_C|MBEDTLS_OID_C|General||||Enable the OID database. Module: library/oid.c Caller: library/asn1write.c library/pkcs5.c library/pkparse.c library/pkwrite.c library/rsa.c library/x509.c library/x509_create.c library/x509_crl.c library/x509_crt.c library/x509_csr.c library/x509write_crt.c library/x509write_csr.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_PADLOCK_C|MBEDTLS_PADLOCK_C|General||||Enable VIA Padlock support on x86. Module: library/padlock.c Caller: library/aes.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_HAVE_ASM
MBEDTLS_PEM_PARSE_C|MBEDTLS_PEM_PARSE_C|General||||Enable PEM decoding / parsing. Module: library/pem.c Caller: library/dhm.c library/pkparse.c library/x509_crl.c library/x509_crt.c library/x509_csr.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_BASE64_C
MBEDTLS_PEM_WRITE_C|MBEDTLS_PEM_WRITE_C|General||||Enable PEM encoding / writing Module: library/pem.c Caller: library/pkwrite.c library/x509write_crt.c library/x509write_csr.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_BASE64_C
MBEDTLS_PK_C|MBEDTLS_PK_C|General||||Enable the generic public (asymetric) key layer. Module: library/pk.c Caller: library/ssl_tls.c library/ssl_cli.c library/ssl_srv.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_RSA_C / MBEDTLS_ECP_C
MBEDTLS_PK_PARSE_C|MBEDTLS_PK_PARSE_C|General||||Enable the generic public (asymetric) key parser. Module: library/pkparse.c Caller: library/x509_crt.c library/x509_csr.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_PK_C
MBEDTLS_PK_WRITE_C|MBEDTLS_PK_WRITE_C|General||||Enable the generic public (asymetric) key writer. Module: library/pkwrite.c Caller: library/x509write.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_PK_C
MBEDTLS_PKCS5_C|MBEDTLS_PKCS5_C|General||||Enable PKCS#5 functions Module: library/pkcs5.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_MD_C
MBEDTLS_PKCS11_C|MBEDTLS_PKCS11_C|General||||Enable wrapper for PKCS#11 smartcard support * Module: library/pkcs11.c Caller: library/pk.c This module enables SSL/TLS PKCS #11 smartcard support. Requires the presence of the PKCS#11 helper library (libpkcs11-helper) <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_PK_C
MBEDTLS_PKCS12_C|MBEDTLS_PKCS12_C|General||||Enable PKCS#12 PBE functions. Adds algorithms for parsing PKCS#8 encrypted private keys Module: library/pkcs12.c Caller: library/pkparse.c Can use: MBEDTLS_ARC4_C This module enables PKCS#12 functions. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ASN1_PARSE_C & MBEDTLS_CIPHER_C & MBEDTLS_MD_C
MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_C|MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_C|General||||Enable the platform abstraction layer that allows you to re-assign functions like calloc(), free(), snprintf(), printf(), fprintf(), exit(). Enabling MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_C enables to use of MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_XXX_ALT or MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_XXX_MACRO directives, allowing the functions mentioned above to be specified at runtime or compile time respectively. <b>Note:</b> This abstraction layer must be enabled on Windows (including MSYS2) as other module rely on it for a fixed snprintf implementation.Module: library/platform.c Caller: Most other .c files <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_POLY1305_C|MBEDTLS_POLY1305_C|General||||Enable the Poly1305 MAC algorithm.. Module: library/poly1305.c Caller: library/chachapoly.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_RIPEMD160_C|MBEDTLS_RIPEMD160_C|General||||Enable the RIPEMD-160 hash algorithm. Module: library/ripemd160.c Caller: library/md.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_RSA_C|MBEDTLS_RSA_C|General||||Enable the RSA public-key cryptosystem Module: library/rsa.c library/rsa_internal.c Caller: library/ssl_cli.c library/ssl_srv.c library/ssl_tls.c library/x509.c This module is used by the following key exchanges: RSA, DHE-RSA, ECDHE-RSA, RSA-PSK <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_BIGNUM_C & MBEDTLS_OID_C
MBEDTLS_SHA1_C|MBEDTLS_SHA1_C|General||||Enable the SHA1 cryptographic hash algorithm Module: library/sha1.c Caller: library/md.c library/ssl_cli.c library/ssl_srv.c library/ssl_tls.c library/x509write_crt.c This module is required for SSL/TLS up to version 1.1, for TLS 1.2 depending on the handshake parameters, and for SHA1-signed certificates. \warning SHA-1 is considered a weak message digest and its use constitutes a security risk. If possible, we recommend avoiding dependencies on it, and considering stronger message digests instead. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SHA256_C|MBEDTLS_SHA256_C|General||||Enable the SHA-224 and SHA-256 cryptographic hash algorithms Module: library/sha256.c Caller: library/entropy.c library/md.clibrary/ssl_cli.c library/ssl_srv.c library/ssl_tls.c This module adds support for SHA-224 and SHA-256. This module is required for the SSL/TLS 1.2 PRF function. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SHA512_C|MBEDTLS_SHA512_C|General||||Enable the SHA-384 and SHA-512 cryptographic hash algorithms Module: library/sha512.c Caller: library/entropy.c library/md.c library/ssl_cli.c library/ssl_srv.c This module adds support for SHA-384 and SHA-512. <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_CACHE_C|MBEDTLS_SSL_CACHE_C|General||||Enable simple SSL cache implementation Module: library/ssl_cache.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_COOKIE_C|MBEDTLS_SSL_COOKIE_C|General||||Enable basic implementation of DTLS cookies for hello verification. Module: library/ssl_cookie.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_SSL_TICKET_C|MBEDTLS_SSL_TICKET_C|General||||Enable an implementation of TLS server-side callbacks for session tickets. Module: library/ssl_ticket.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_CIPHER_C
MBEDTLS_SSL_CLI_C|MBEDTLS_SSL_CLI_C|Modes||||Enable the SSL/TLS client code Module: library/ssl_cli.c <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS_C
MBEDTLS_SSL_SRV_C|MBEDTLS_SSL_SRV_C|Modes||||Enable the SSL/TLS server code Module: library/ssl_srv.c <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS_C
MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS_C|MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS_C|General||||Enable the generic SSL/TLS code Module: library/ssl_tls.c Caller: library/ssl_cli.c library/ssl_srv.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_CIPHER_C & MBEDTLS_MD_C & (MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_SSL3 / MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1 / MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_1 / MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_DTLS)
MBEDTLS_THREADING_C|MBEDTLS_THREADING_C|General||||Need FreeRTOS to be activated - Enable the threading abstraction layer. By default mbed TLS assumes it is used in a non-threaded environment or that contexts are not shared between threads. If you do intend to use contexts between threads, you will need to enable this layer to prevent race conditions.See also our Knowledge Base article about threading: https://tls.mbed.org/kb/development/thread-safety-and-multi-threading Module: library/threading.c This allows different threading implementations (self-implemented or provided). You will have to enable either MBEDTLS_THREADING_ALT or MBEDTLS_THREADING_PTHREAD. <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_TIMING_C|MBEDTLS_TIMING_C|General||||Enable the portable timing interface <b>Note:</b>The provided implementation only works on POSIX/Unix (including Linux,BSD and OS X) and Windows. On other platforms, you can either disable thatodule and provide your own implementations of the callbacks needed by \c mbedtls_ssl_set_timer_cb() for DTLS, or leave it enabled and provide your own implementation of the whole module by setting \c MBEDTLS_TIMING_ALT in the current file. <b>Note:</b> See also our Knowledge Base article about porting to a new environment: https://tls.mbed.org/kb/how-to/how-do-i-port-mbed-tls-to-a-new-environment-OS Module: library/timing.c Caller: library/havege.c <b>Default value: </b>Not Defined(//#define)
MBEDTLS_VERSION_C|MBEDTLS_VERSION_C|General||||Enable run-time version information Module: library/version.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_X509_USE_C|MBEDTLS_X509_USE_C|General||||Enable X.509 core for using certificates. Module: library/x509.c Caller: library/x509_crl.c library/x509_crt.c library/x509_csr.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_ASN1_PARSE_C & MBEDTLS_BIGNUM_C & MBEDTLS_OID_C & MBEDTLS_PK_PARSE_C
MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_PARSE_C|MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_PARSE_C|General||||Enable X.509 certificate parsing. Module: library/x509_crt.c Caller: library/ssl_cli.c library/ssl_srv.c library/ssl_tls.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_X509_USE_C
MBEDTLS_X509_CRL_PARSE_C|MBEDTLS_X509_CRL_PARSE_C|General||||Enable X.509 CRL parsing. Module: library/x509_crl.c Caller: library/x509_crt.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_X509_USE_C
MBEDTLS_X509_CSR_PARSE_C|MBEDTLS_X509_CSR_PARSE_C|General||||Enable X.509 Certificate Signing Request (CSR) parsing. Module: library/x509_csr.c Caller: library/x509_crt_write.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_X509_USE_C
MBEDTLS_X509_CREATE_C|MBEDTLS_X509_CREATE_C|General||||Enable X.509 core for creating certificates. Module: library/x509_create.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_BIGNUM_C & MBEDTLS_OID_C & MBEDTLS_PK_WRITE_C
MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_WRITE_C|MBEDTLS_X509_CRT_WRITE_C|General||||Enable creating X.509 certificates. Module: library/x509_crt_write.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_X509_CREATE_C
MBEDTLS_X509_CSR_WRITE_C|MBEDTLS_X509_CSR_WRITE_C|General||||Enable creating X.509 Certificate Signing Requests (CSR). Module: library/x509_csr_write.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define) <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_X509_CREATE_C
MBEDTLS_XTEA_C|MBEDTLS_XTEA_C|General||||Enable the XTEA block cipher Module: library/xtea.c <b>Default value:</b> Defined(#define)
MBEDTLS_MPI_WINDOW_SIZE_ENABLE|MBEDTLS_MPI_WINDOW_SIZE_ENABLE|MPI / BIGNUM||||Enable MBEDTLS_MPI_WINDOW_SIZE options configuration <b>Default value: </b>Disabled <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_BIGNUM_C
MBEDTLS_MPI_WINDOW_SIZE|MBEDTLS_MPI_WINDOW_SIZE|MPI / BIGNUM||||Maximum windows size used <b>Default value:</b> 6
MBEDTLS_MPI_MAX_SIZE_ENABLE|MBEDTLS_MPI_MAX_SIZE_ENABLE|MPI / BIGNUM||||Enable MBEDTLS_MPI_MAX_SIZE options configuration<b> Default value: </b>Disabled <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_BIGNUM_C
MBEDTLS_MPI_MAX_SIZE|MBEDTLS_MPI_MAX_SIZE|MPI / BIGNUM||||Maximum number of bytes for usable MPIs <b>Default value:</b> 1024
MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_ENTROPY_LEN_ENABLE|MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_ENTROPY_LEN_ENABLE|CTR_DRBG||||Enable MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_ENTROPY_LEN options configuration <b>Default value: </b>Disabled <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_C
MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_ENTROPY_LEN|MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_ENTROPY_LEN|CTR_DRBG||||Amount of entropy used per seed by default (48 with SHA-512, 32 with SHA-256) <b>Default value:</b> 48
MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_RESEED_INTERVAL_ENABLE|MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_RESEED_INTERVAL_ENABLE|CTR_DRBG||||Enable MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_RESEED_INTERVAL options configuration <b>Default value: </b>Disabled <b>Require:</b> MBEDTLS_CTR_DRBG_C
